<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Nlp on Best of AI</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tags/nlp/</link><description>Recent content in Nlp on Best of AI</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://bestofai.io/tags/nlp/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>BERT</title><link>https://bestofai.io/models/bert/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/models/bert/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers) is a language model that Google Research published in October 2018, and it changed how the field approached pretraining for NLP tasks. Unlike earlier models that read text left to right, BERT trains on masked-word prediction and next-sentence prediction, letting it build representations that draw on context from both directions at once. Google released two main sizes: BERT-base at 110 million parameters and BERT-large at 340 million, both with a 512-token limit, and made the weights freely available under Apache 2.0 on GitHub and later Hugging Face. Fine-tuned versions of BERT set new records on eleven different NLP benchmarks at launch, including question answering and natural language inference, and it quickly became the standard base model to fine-tune for tasks like classification, named entity recognition, and search ranking. It&amp;rsquo;s mostly been superseded by newer encoder models like RoBERTa and DeBERTa and by the embedding models that followed it, but it&amp;rsquo;s still one of the most cited papers in NLP and its architecture underlies a large share of later encoder-based systems.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>T5</title><link>https://bestofai.io/models/t5/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/models/t5/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Bloomfire</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/bloomfire/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/bloomfire/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Haystack</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/haystack/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/haystack/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Hex</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/hex/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/hex/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Landbot</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/landbot/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/landbot/</guid><description/></item><item><title>MotherDuck</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/motherduck/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/motherduck/</guid><description/></item><item><title>ScrapeGraph AI</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/scrapegraph-ai/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/scrapegraph-ai/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Clarifai</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/clarifai/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/clarifai/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Lexalytics</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/lexalytics/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/lexalytics/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Stats Perform</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/stats-perform/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/stats-perform/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Causal</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/causal-app/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/causal-app/</guid><description/></item><item><title>ChatGPT</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/chatgpt/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/chatgpt/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;ChatGPT launched in November 2022 and reached a million users in five days, faster than any consumer product before it. It runs on OpenAI&amp;rsquo;s GPT-4o model, which handles text, images, files, and voice inside a single conversation thread. The interface is approachable enough for someone who&amp;rsquo;s never used AI before, yet the underlying capabilities are deep enough that developers, lawyers, analysts, and writers treat it as a daily work tool.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Claap</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/claap/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/claap/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Claude</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/claude/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/claude/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Claude is built by Anthropic, a safety-focused AI company co-founded by former OpenAI researchers. Where many AI assistants optimise for engagement, Claude is designed to be genuinely helpful without being agreeable to the point of dishonesty: it pushes back, admits uncertainty, and declines requests it considers harmful. That combination of directness and reliability has made it a favourite among people who use AI for serious work rather than casual queries.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Clockwise</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/clockwise-ai/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/clockwise-ai/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Gemini</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Gemini is Google&amp;rsquo;s answer to ChatGPT, and what sets it apart is how deeply it&amp;rsquo;s woven into products people already use every day. It sits inside Gmail to help draft and summarise emails, inside Google Docs to rewrite and restructure text, inside Google Meet to take notes, and inside Android to respond to voice queries. For anyone already living in the Google ecosystem, Gemini often shows up exactly where the work is happening rather than requiring a separate tab.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Gemini Advanced</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini-advanced/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/gemini-advanced/</guid><description/></item><item><title>GitLens AI</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/gitlens-ai/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/gitlens-ai/</guid><description/></item><item><title>GPT Engineer</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/gptengineer/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/gptengineer/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Harvey</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/harvey/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/harvey/</guid><description/></item><item><title>IBM Watson Government</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/ibm-watson-gov/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/ibm-watson-gov/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Kensho</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/kensho/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/kensho/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Kimi</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/kimi/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bestofai.io/tools/kimi/</guid><description/></item><item><title>LangChain</title><link>https://bestofai.io/tools/langchain/</link><pub